sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch02-13> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Computers are not limited to computing the consequences of mathematical equations; directly studying the behavior of even the simplest computer programs yields fundamental scientific discoveries.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Computers enable discoveries beyond working out mathematical equations";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 2, “The Crucial Experiment”; section “Why These Discoveries Were Not Made Before” (from p. 42), p. 45. Scope: the role of computers in basic science"
}
